# Split action (standard)

One purple control: the primary button on the left, a full-height divider, and the ⋮ menu on the right.
Each half gets a white-tint hover. Outer corners rounded, inner corners square.

```html
<span class="split-action">
  <p-button label="Save" icon="pi pi-check" (onClick)="save()" />
  <app-row-actions-menu class="split-action-more" [attached]="true" [items]="menu()" ariaLabel="More client actions" />
</span>
```

- **Reuse, don't rebuild:** the ⋮ half is `app-row-actions-menu` with `[attached]="true"` (same popover, items, separators). Styles: `assets/layout/_split-action.scss` plus the attached styles in the menu component.
- Menu order: actions closest to the primary first, then a separator, then page-wide actions.
- When the primary isn't shown (e.g. another tab), show the plain `app-row-actions-menu` on its own.
- Use it on every page header that has a primary button and a ⋮ menu. Secondary outlined buttons (Open form, Discard, Reopen…) stay separate, to the left.
- The primary half can be `<p-button>` or `<a pButton>`.
- Used on: Client detail, Lead detail, Pipeline board, Project edit, Task Manager project, Task form builder, Form submission, Client form result, Care visit, Booking type edit, Invoice edit, Invoice detail.
